<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.9.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00212</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.9.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>edfc1b6b-2953-48fe-ba03-6f2f7a244115</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For numbers 1 – 9, use the following scenario:</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="7549e8cd-9305-465b-b608-5ac053024935" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Enter Questions Below this line-->
  <!--1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c9c0b944-2eb3-43b2-acc4-79148148453b" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="30">
    <problem>
      <para>How many miles has the car traveled if it has 15 gallons left in the tank?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 30 miles</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0b8af3c9-6742-4109-9f34-7f7fab8f173e" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="180">
    <problem>
      <para>How many miles has the car traveled if it has 10 gallons left in the tank?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 180 miles</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2ab2e5e8-03f0-40d4-898e-c6155a3fe6c4" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="405">
    <problem>
      <para>How many miles has the car traveled if it has 2.5 gallons left in the tank?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 405 miles</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="97d672df-68be-43e5-8182-3eeb958b2ccd" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(d=30(16-x)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(d=16(30-x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=\\frac{d-480}{-30}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d=30(16-x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=\\frac{30}{d-480}\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose the equation that represents the relationship between the distance the car has traveled in miles, \(d\),
          and the amount of gas left in the tank in gallons, \(x\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(d=30(16-x)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="6b70c89b-27d4-46db-830d-6009497c889c" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="13">
    <problem>
      <para>How many gallons are left in the tank when the car has traveled 90 miles?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 13 gallons</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0c673f94-e584-4e9e-a231-7697c0dba0dc" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="7.8">
    <problem>
      <para>How many gallons are left in the tank when the car has traveled 246 miles?
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 7.8 gallons</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3480b5d0-91da-4121-bd45-5ab49f90db3c" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(x=\frac{d-480}{-30}\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(d=16(30-x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=\\frac{d-480}{-30}\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(d=30(16-x)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x=\\frac{30}{d-480}\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Choose an equation
          that makes it easier to find the amount of gas left in the tank, \(x\), if we know the car has traveled \(d\) miles.
        </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(x=\frac{d-480}{-30}\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="c4617740-0dff-4561-ab05-fbbbcf1b0df6" data-problem-type="multiselect" data-solution="[&quot;\\( 281.25 - 5.25a=2.75s \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(a=53.57- \\frac{2.75}{5.25}s\\)&quot;]" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\( 281.25 - 5.25a=2.75s \\)&quot;, &quot;\\(a=53.57- \\frac{2.75}{5.25}s\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x - 2 =4\\)&quot;,&quot;\\(x - 2 = 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(x -6 = 4\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Noah was helping to collect the entry fees at his school's football game. Student entry costs $2.75 each and adult
          entry costs $5.25 each. By the end of the game, Diego had collected $281.25.
        </para>
      <para><emphasis>Select two </emphasis>equations that could represent the relationship between the number of students, \(s\), the number of adults, \(a\), and the dollar amount collected at the game.
      </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \( 281.25 - 5.25a=2.75s \), \(a=53.57- \frac{2.75}{5.25}s \)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.9.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
